<title>USA: Invacare boosts Healthdyne offer to $13/shr.</title>
<headline>Invacare boosts Healthdyne offer to $13/shr.</headline>
<dateline>ELYRIA, Ohio 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Invacare Corp said it increased its all-cash tender offer for Healthdyne Technologies Inc to $13 per share.</p>
<p>The company said the offer is a $0.50 per share increase over its original acquisition proposal on January 2, which Healthdyne's board rejected. Invacare said that in light of that rejection, it is making this proposal directly to Healthdyne's shareholders.</p>
<p>Invacare also said that it sued Healthdyne to prevent Healthdyne from adopting a poison pill defense.</p>
